Hi

Yes, providing a reproducible example <https://stackoverflow.com/questions/5963269/how-to-make-a-great-r-reproducible-example> would help us to help you. It seems the problem comes from the fact that your input data is in a tibble format... strange, but at least that what happens in the example below. So simple solution would be just to use as.data.frame():
da.imp=imputeFAMD(as.data.frame(DA),ncp=2)

## Example using dataset diamonds:
library(missMDA)
library(tidyverse)

data(diamonds)
diamonds[c(3, 5), c(2,3)] <-  NA

head(imputeFAMD(head(diamonds, 1000), ncp=3)$completeObs)
head(imputeFAMD(as.data.frame(head(diamonds, 1000)), ncp=3)$completeObs)

# first one gives all vector of NA, seoncd one not...

Does this help

Matthieu

