Michael Koontz and I are putting together a Carpentries workshop with the newly finished Geospatial Curriculum.  It will be a 2-day workshop on Nov. 29-30 in Valley Hall on the west side of the main UCD campus.  We need a few more co-instructors and helpers for this workshop.  You don’t need to be a certified Carpentries instructor to participate.  We need people with plain R (for the intro to R lessons) and geospatial R (for the geospatial lessons) experience.

More information:  https://mikoontz.github.io/2018-11-29-davis-geospatial/

Want to be an instructor or helper?  Email me!

Want to attend the workshop to learn?  I’ll be sending out the registration information very soon, so stay tuned to the geospatial or D-RUG email lists!

Best,

