From ub35e99045f6c74c2 at groups.google.com  Tue Oct 30 15:53:10 2018
From: ub35e99045f6c74c2 at groups.google.com (Vince S. Buffalo)
Date: Tue, 30 Oct 2018 15:53:10 +0000
Subject: Re: [D-RUG]: R: How to cbind 2 data frames in this specific case
Message-ID: <CVrWgsdrkJw.8wsYR2gRAQAJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <CVrWgsdrkJw.41fzDh8RAQAJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
References: <CVrWgsdrkJw.41fzDh8RAQAJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/davis-rug/c/CVrWgsdrkJw/m/8wsYR2gRAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I think you're looking for a left join <https://dplyr.tidyverse.org/reference/join.html>; the best implementation is in tidyverse:

v<-c(rep(1, times=3), rep(2, times=3), rep(3, times=3))
a <- data.frame("x" = rep(c(10:12), times=3), "y"=v, "NDVI" = rep(c("0.5", "0.6", "0.7"), times=3))

w<-c(rep(3, times=3), rep(4, times=3), rep(5, times=3))
b <- data.frame("x" = rep(c(10:12), times=3), "y"=w, "NDVI" = rep(c("0.8", "0.9", "0.95"), times=3))

library(tidyverse)
left_join(a, b, by=c('x', 'y'))
   x y NDVI.x NDVI.y

1 10 1    0.5   <NA>
2 11 1    0.6   <NA>
3 12 1    0.7   <NA>
4 10 2    0.5   <NA>
5 11 2    0.6   <NA>
6 12 2    0.7   <NA>
7 10 3    0.5    0.8

8 11 3    0.6    0.9

9 12 3    0.7   0.95

Hope this helps,
Vince

